            <div xml:id="d825-a1">

                <pb facs="0975" n="895" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg895"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Demonetization of soles.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Treasury Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-01-17"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">January 17,
                    1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>For the due carrying into effect of article 4 of the transitory law of December
                    14, 1901, it is resolved: <list>
                        <item>First. The treasury department shall order the smelting into silver
                            bars at the national mint of 500,000 entire soles—silver-coined
                            money.</item>
                        <item>Second. The said department shall take measures to have these bars
                            exported to Europe and sold there, and shall employ the product of the
                            same in the importation of gold.</item>
                        <item>Third. The expenses attached to these operations shall be chargeable
                            to item 5495 of the present budget on account of
                            “demonetization.”</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>[The rubric of His Excellency.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ward.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
